    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d127">

                <pb facs="0181" n="91" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg91"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1367</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Spencer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-03-26T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 26, 1918,
                                noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 26,
                            7.43 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following from Harbin just received: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Drysdale and Morton telegraphed March 24 prisoners at Chita and northward
                            armed, committing misdeeds. Contrary to orders of German and Austrian
                            officers, very few are joining Red Guard.</p></quote></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Spencer</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
